c5c53579b62cfd0d8725cca60bde9582dfc2594dd8f2b89328d48f9def465","event_uuid":"870d8293-8a1b-4935-9c5d-54cca06de19f","position":{"commit_sha":"889b12a9981d809136707375b434a90c91bed2bd","position":"1787740275027945001-870d8293-8a1b-4935-9c5d-54cca06de19f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9e0cf52b80c598f929abe07faa77b9868611c143b268de42f4ea89bd15aeecd1","event_uuid":"a18f52bc-a5bd-4a27-b3e5-6a8fd4364728","position":{"commit_sha":"7bae4c5eae98b6d7af3e8ee2e988a77888348ac9","position":"1787740296845901001-a18f52bc-a5bd-4a27-b3e5-6a8fd4364728"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented + independently validated. Diff = exactly the 6 file_impact paths. Full tests/unit/rebar_reconciler: 3584 passed/1 skipped. make lint + make typecheck green. LOC: reconcile 796, manifest_renderer 381, last_pass 405 (all <800). Teeth: perturbing mutations_recovered->0 makes test_mixed_pass_tally_is_exact_including_recovered go RED (assert 0==5); reverted. AC1 hash pinned to concrete golden ad5bfa39...9f83d; render_pass_outcomes is a pure sibling section leaving serialize_manifest bytes/hash identical. Write-boundary repair stays after ensure_selection_current and before first remote fetch (guard suite green). Rebased onto current origin/main (clean, no conflicts). Pushed Gerrit change 2238.","timestamp":1787730777647242001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LLM-Review ps2 = BLOCK (-1). Blocking (correctness): the AC5 comment claimed recovered was un-folded from applied, but on the real cutover path mutations_applied still included recovered (double-count vs the new mutations_recovered field). Root cause: derive_pass_tally's applied is the LEGACY folded count — build_pass_tally sets applied_count=applied+recovered (pinned by test_build_pass_tally_folds_recovered_into_applied) and the non-error manifest count includes recovered outcomes. Fix (ps3, reconcile.py only — build_pass_tally's fold is an intentional legacy-consumer contract left intact): mutations_applied = max(0, tally['applied'] - recovered_count), un-folding downstream so the five reported buckets are DISJOINT and sum to mutation_count (AC5 exact tallies). RED-first: test_mixed_pass_tally_is_exact_including_recovered rewritten to the production-folded shape (applied_count 9 = 4 applied + 5 recovered) asserting mutations_applied==4 + exactness; NEW test_reconcile_unfolds_the_real_build_pass_tally_fold drives a real CutoverReport through build_pass_tally into reconcile (addresses the advisory that the old test used a synthetic independent shape). Both seen RED (5==3) then GREEN. Regression: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler + interfaces/facades + interfaces/contracts = 4558 passed/2 skipped; lint+typecheck green; reconcile 798 LOC (<800).","timestamp":1787736508391309001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close evidence (change 2238 MERGED, LLM-Review +1 PASS + Verified +1): all 11 ACs satisfied. Core: canonical hash/array bytes unchanged + additive versioned output + no-secrets manifests (test_bridge_canonical_manifest + test_bridge_status[_heldout] 24 passed); cursor/baseline advance only on proven postconditions (test_preview_lifecycle_intents 7 passed); disjoint eligibility + exact mixed-pass tallies via the recovered un-fold in reconcile (test_live_mode_failure_tally 21 passed incl the real-build_pass_tally anchor). Inherited boundary invariant: repair stays AFTER ensure_selection_current and BEFORE first remote fetch, re-anchored (test_recovery_write_boundary 21 passed); reconcile.py 798 LOC (<800). CI full-suite is the ultimate oracle (Verified +1). Advisory (non-blocking, deferred to residual-gap sweep): manifest_renderer.render_pass_outcomes truncates fuse_state silently without a fuse_state_truncated count.","timestamp":1787740000474949001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787028466987207001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"117d0b76-d030-41fe-8e09-b824ca33c5f6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d7b9-ac42-ad6f-4608"},{"link_uuid":"d3660bdd-d702-480c-8dd9-21d6edcff2ed","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"674c-f0ad-00f3-44bb"},{"link_uuid":"af91bd5c-8b02-4d68-84cc-6fa798e7a2d5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5fc0-3207-fbcf-424b"},{"link_uuid":"ccba457a-11d4-435f-8c3f-8c5bd1eb969f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"856b-380c-30ed-4254"}],"description":"## Context\nOnce coordinator results are authoritative, preview/log/manifest consumers need a stable additive contract and state must advance only for proven postconditions. Deferred or ambiguous work cannot be reported as applied.\n\n## Outcome\nFinalize versioned lifecycle/retry/fuse outcome sections, exact pass tallies/cursor behavior, and redacted bounded diagnostics while preserving existing mutation fields.\n\n## Plan\n1. Render versioned lifecycle intents, logical/physical attempts, delay source/value, budget, failure scope, disposition, `retry_not_before`, fuse state, and exact ticket/pass outcomes.\n2. Preserve the existing mutation fields/array/hash and make additive sections ignorable by older readers.\n3. Advance cursor, baseline, binding, and last-pass state only after proven postconditions. Deferred, failed, skipped, and `commit_unknown` work stays eligible for later re-observation.\n4. Pin applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered tallies and exit semantics for mixed passes and delivery failure.\n5. Redact secrets and bound every diagnostic field and collection.\n\n## Testing\nGolden preview/log/manifest fixtures cover every disposition and mixed pass. State spies assert exact writes and next-pass eligibility.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Existing mutation fields, array bytes, and canonical hash remain unchanged.\n- [x] Additive versioned output includes every named lifecycle/retry/fuse/outcome field.\n- [x] Cursor, baseline, and binding state advance only for proven postconditions.\n- [x] Deferred, failed, skipped, and `commit_unknown` work is not counted as applied and remains eligible next pass.\n- [x] Mixed-pass tallies and exit status are exact.\n- [x] Logs and manifests contain no secret or unbounded diagnostic content.\n\n## Out of scope\nRoute removal and portable end-to-end/documentation completion.\n\n## Inherited invariant — pre-observation repair boundary (folded in from insectile-modest-martin, 2026-08-19)\n\nOperator decision: `insectile-modest-martin` (d7b9-ac42) is CLOSED and its requirement now lives\nhere. This ticket edits `reconcile.py`, which sits at **799 of the 800-line cap**, so it must\nperform a behaviour-preserving extraction (extract along an existing call-graph seam; NEVER raise\nthe limit). That extraction must preserve one specific ordering invariant that is easy to break\nsilently.\n\n**The invariant.** The call\n`binding_store.repair_at_write_boundary(persist=persist, scoped=bool(scoped_ids))` must remain:\n\n- **AFTER** the under-lock staleness validation (`ensure_selection_current`) — a pass whose\n  selection is stale has not established that its view is current and has no standing to repair; and\n- **BEFORE** the pass's first remote issue fetch (`fetcher.fetch_snapshot` / `compute_snapshot`).\n\nThe pre-observation half is the one with teeth. A durable tombstone is authoritative retirement\nintent. A pass that fetched first could observe the retired issue answer 200 and then complete that\nissue's retirement in the same breath as fresh evidence that it is alive; repairing first keeps the\nrecorded decision from racing a later observation. **Move the call after the fetch and the repair\nstill runs, still writes correct-looking bytes, and is silently wrong.**\n\n`run_differs.py` is specifically NOT an alternative home: `reconcile._load_snapshots` performs the\nfirst remote fetch inside itself, and both `bind_operation_runtime` and `run_differs()` run after it\nreturns, so no position inside `run_differs.py` can precede remote observation. Recorded in ADR 0099.\n\n**The two tests that are the only guard** (both drive or name `_load_snapshots` directly, so an\nextraction that renames or re-splits that phase WILL force someone to touch them) — in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py`:\n\n- `test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation` — the behavioural oracle; drives the real\n  load phase with an event recorder and asserts the repair event precedes the fetch event.\n- `test_the_repair_is_invoked_from_reconcile_and_not_from_run_differs` — a structural anchor.\n\nThe tempting shortcut under time pressure is to relax the assertion rather than re-anchor it.\n**Relaxing it is the thing to avoid.**\n\n### Additional acceptance criteria (inherited)\n- [x] After this change to `reconcile.py`, the repair call still runs after the under-lock staleness\n      gate and before the pass's first remote issue fetch.\n- [x] `test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation` still fails when the call is moved to a\n      post-fetch position — demonstrated by SEEDING that move and observing RED, not merely by the\n      suite being green.\n- [x] If the load phase is renamed or re-split, the boundary tests are RE-ANCHORED to the new\n      structure rather than relaxed, and the ordering assertion survives in a form that still\n      discriminates.\n- [x] `reconcile.py` remains within the 800-line cap without raising the limit.\n- [x] ADR 0099's invocation-boundary section is updated if the realized position changes shape.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/manifest_renderer.py","reason":"Seal versioned lifecycle, retry, fuse, and outcome output."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"Advance state and exit status from proven coordinator outcomes."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py","reason":"Persist exact deferred, failed, and recovered pass semantics."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_preview_lifecycle_intents.py","reason":"Golden additive preview and redaction contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_bridge_canonical_manifest.py","reason":"Existing mutation field and hash compatibility."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py","reason":"State advancement, exact tally, and exit regressions."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status.py","reason":"Fresh last-pass write now carries schema_version 2 (additive advance)."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3350-90b1-2651-4c50"],["relates_to","5fc0-3207-fbcf-424b"],["relates_to","674c-f0ad-00f3-44bb"],["relates_to","856b-380c-30ed-4254"],["relates_to","d7b9-ac42-ad6f-4608"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3350-90b1-2651-4c50","parent_status_uuid":"870d8293-8a1b-4935-9c5d-54cca06de19f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp03","manifest","reconciler","tdd"],"ticket_id":"0f5d-2a24-91d2-4148","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S5 T2 — Seal versioned outcomes and proven-state advancement","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_preview_lifecycle_intents.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_bridge_canonical_manifest.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC2,AC6","dd_text":"Mutation compatibility, additive versioned output, and bounded redaction"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py","dd_id":"AC3-AC5","dd_text":"Proven-only state advancement, next-pass eligibility, exact tallies, and exit"}]},"source_event_uuids":["117d0b76-d030-41fe-8e09-b824ca33c5f6","e9ec57ff-497b-4151-88b5-dfa7ae684716","830225e8-f014-437b-b1bd-f5d883fed505","724ac354-cf31-4dfb-aee9-501fc01d0d80","7ae0c738-1eeb-44ac-ac6a-17bb37fc7e23","282d4160-d1ce-4e85-8dd6-2f8f4ba5a8e4","c728ee69-df1d-472a-8c5b-a0640995d9fd","d3660bdd-d702-480c-8dd9-21d6edcff2ed","78bf2134-26e5-48ca-ac9b-3eeefddd3e05","af91bd5c-8b02-4d68-84cc-6fa798e7a2d5","ccba457a-11d4-435f-8c3f-8c5bd1eb969f","755d0c42-5968-4d5b-a5b2-567c248e59f6","e84b7a2a-c8e0-4a70-8316-49432dec16ef","8fbceda8-2359-468b-b46d-d446d58013b4","870d8293-8a1b-4935-9c5d-54cca06de19f","a18f52bc-a5bd-4a27-b3e5-6a8fd4364728"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787744978078226001,"uuid":"9f35f7d0-66ee-448a-813b-9d7fa4a5e9f2"}